# Vendor access — no seam files in `app/components/`

## Layout

| Location | Contents |
| -------- | -------- |
| `app/vendor/` | Upstream bytes only (UMD bundles, ESM trees, README pins). Never our wrappers or version helpers. |
| `app/components/<id>.js` | Product component: owns vendor access, documents load order, exports pinned version constants when useful. |
| `app/utils/` | Shared infra only — extract a vendor helper here **only** when **two or more** components need the same accessors. |

## Do

- Access UMD globals from the component (`window.Prism`, `window.toastui`, …) with a readiness check before use
- Import vendored ESM with relative paths from the component (and document any import-map bare specifiers in the component header)
- Keep version pins / refresh notes in the component file header (or exported `*_VERSION` consts), matching the catalogue id

## Do not

- Add a per-vendor seam file under `app/components/` (e.g. `toastui-editor.js`, `prism.js`, `tanstack-charts.js`) when only one component uses that vendor
- Put framework-owned adapter code inside `app/vendor/`
- Invent a second access pattern for a new vendor — follow the owning component

## When a shared seam is justified

If a second component needs the same vendor API, move the accessors to `app/utils/<name>.js` (infrastructure layer), not a new file in `app/components/`. Keep the product `initX` modules thin wrappers around that helper.

## Examples in this repo

- **Prism** — `code-block.js` reads `window.Prism` directly
- **Toast UI** — `rich-text-editor.js` owns `window.toastui` access and `TOASTUI_EDITOR_VERSION`
- **TanStack Charts** (when present) — `charts.js` imports from `app/vendor/tanstack-charts/` and pins versions there
- **Mermaid** (when present) — `diagram.js` imports from `app/vendor/mermaid/` and pins `MERMAID_VERSION` there
